.TH HOUSEKEEPER 6 "2026-10-30" "housekeeper 1.2.0" "Games Manual"
.
.SH NAME
housekeeper \- defend a carpet from dripping burgers and spilling martinis
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B housekeeper
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B housekeeper
is a Space Invaders variant.
A grid of forty invaders \(em twenty martini glasses in the top two rows and
twenty burgers in the bottom two \(em marches back and forth across a
living room, descending one notch each time it reaches a wall.
The martinis spill drops and the burgers drip blobs of fat.
Anything that reaches the floor stains the carpet.
.PP
You are the housekeeper.
Move along the bottom of the room and shoot the invaders with your spray
bottle before their droppings ruin the carpet, and mop up the stains that
do land.
Four mid-century modern credenzas stand between you and the grid; they
absorb droppings (and your own shots), show the stains, and collapse after
four hits.
From time to time a Bloody Mary drifts across the top of the room,
dropping a single large splash of tomato juice on its way; shooting it is
worth a bonus.
.PP
Clearing the grid starts the next wave: the furniture is restored and you
gain a life, but the carpet stays as you left it, and the invaders are
faster and drop more.
The game ends only when you lose.
.PP
The game is rendered entirely with SDL2 primitives and procedurally
generated 8-bit sound.
It has no external assets and the same source compiles natively and to
WebAssembly.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-difficulty " " \fIN\fR
Start immediately at difficulty
.I N
(1 = easy, 2 = medium, 3 = hard, 4 = nightmare), skipping the selection
screen.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-fullscreen
Start in fullscreen.
The 900\(mu650 playfield is letterboxed to the display.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mute
Start with sound muted.
.B M
toggles sound at any time.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.
.SH CONTROLS
.SS Selection screen
.TP
.BR Up / Down ", " W / S
Move the cursor.
.TP
.BR 1 \(en 4
Select that difficulty and start at once.
.TP
.BR Enter ", " Space
Start at the highlighted difficulty.
.TP
.B Esc
Quit.
.SS In game
.TP
.BR Left / Right ", " A / D
Move the housekeeper.
.TP
.B Space
Fire.
The number of shots that may be in flight at once, and the reload delay
between shots, depend on the difficulty (see below).
A yellow bar under the housekeeper shows the reload progress when a delay
applies.
Holding the key autofires at the reload rate.
.TP
.BR Down ", " S
Mop.
Stand still over a stain and hold the key; after about a second the stain
is gone and you score 5 points.
Moving, releasing the key, or being hit cancels the mop.
You cannot fire while mopping.
.TP
.B P
Pause and resume.
.TP
.B M
Mute and unmute.
.TP
.B F
Toggle fullscreen.
.TP
.B Esc
Abandon the game and return to the selection screen.
.SS Between waves
.TP
.BR Enter ", " Space
Start the next wave at once instead of waiting.
.SS After a game
.TP
.BR R ", " Enter
Return to the selection screen.
.SS Gamepad
Any controller SDL recognises works, and may be plugged in at any time.
Left stick or D-pad moves (down mops);
.B A
fires or confirms,
.B B
is Esc,
.B X
pauses,
.B Y
mutes,
.B Start
is Enter and
.B Back
toggles fullscreen.
.
.SH RULES
.SS Waves
Destroying all forty invaders clears the wave.
The next wave begins after a short pause with new invaders and fresh
credenzas; the carpet stains, your score and your lives carry over, and you
gain one life (up to five).
Each wave the grid starts 10% faster (down to a floor) and one more
dropping may be in the air at once.
.SS Losing
Any one of:
.IP \(bu 3
The soil meter on the left edge fills: thirty droppings have reached the
carpet.
.IP \(bu 3
You lose all three lives.
A dropping that hits you costs a life and also stains the carpet.
.IP \(bu 3
A living invader reaches the carpet.
.SS Scoring
.TS
l l.
Martini glass	20 points
Burger	10 points
Mopped stain	5 points
Bloody Mary	50, 100 or 150 points
.TE
.PP
The best score for each difficulty is kept (see
.BR FILES ).
.SS Pace
Each kill speeds up the grid.
Droppings fall only from the lowest living invader in a column, and the
number that may be in the air at once grows from one to five as the grid
thins (plus one per wave, to a maximum of six).
.SS The Bloody Mary
Every 12 to 24 seconds a Bloody Mary crosses the lane above the grid in a
random direction and drops one large splash at a random point.
The splash counts as two stains on the carpet, or two if it hits you.
Shoot the glass before it leaves the screen for the bonus shown.
.
.SH DIFFICULTY
.TS
l l l l.
Level	Shots in flight	Reload	Grid step
_
Easy	3	none	1200 ms
Medium	2	250 ms	900 ms
Hard	1	600 ms	900 ms
Nightmare	1	1200 ms	650 ms
.TE
.PP
Reload is the minimum interval between consecutive shots; grid step is the
interval between invader moves at the start of a game, falling to 100 ms as
the grid empties.
.
.SH STRATEGY
Thin the grid from the outside in: a narrower grid spends more steps
between wall bounces and therefore descends more slowly.
Clear the bottom rows first; droppings come only from the lowest invader in
each column, and burgers are the easier targets.
Stand behind a credenza when several droppings are falling, and do not
fire until a lane is clear \(em a wasted shot on the harder levels leaves
you defenceless for over a second.
Mop during the lull right after a wave starts, while the grid is still
high and slow; later in a wave a second standing still is a second too
long.
Never let the Bloody Mary's splash land: two stains at once is the
fastest way to fill the meter.
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.
.TP
.B 1
SDL could not be initialised or no window or renderer could be created.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line option.
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B housekeeper
honours the usual SDL2 environment variables, in particular
.B SDL_VIDEODRIVER
and
.BR SDL_AUDIODRIVER .
Running with
.B SDL_AUDIODRIVER=dummy
disables sound entirely on systems with no audio device; the game then
starts normally and reports the condition once on standard error.
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/housekeeper/hiscore
.TQ
.I ~/.local/state/housekeeper/hiscore
Best score for each difficulty, four integers on one line (easy to
nightmare).
The directory is created on first save.
Delete the file to reset the scores.
The browser build keeps the same four values in the page's
.IR localStorage .
.
.SH BUGS
The native build caps its frame rate at roughly 60 Hz with a fixed
16 ms sleep; on displays with a higher refresh rate movement is still
smooth because all motion is time-based, but presentation is not
synchronised to the display.
.PP
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/micomrkaic/carpet_defense/issues
.UE .
.
